summary:
  The directory lookup refuses to knock with a bare return, leaving the
  standing order armed with no ladder under it.

history:
  This is the half the first fix missed, found the same evening by re-reading
  the change rather than the intention behind it. _healArmRetry got the
  teardown; _tryHealStation kept a bare return one guard earlier — and that
  is the branch the DEFAULT configuration takes. Address healing is on out of
  the box, so a listener who unticks the retry switch reaches line 4143 and
  never reaches the ladder at all: the order stays up, no timer is armed, no
  word is shown, and the next reachability edge hands a station that died
  hours ago to netResumeTimer. Issue #13 verbatim, under the very setting
  offered as its cure. The function's own comment, six lines above, states
  the contract the bare return broke: every early return past that point
  still owes the standing order a heartbeat.

target:
  package/contents/ui/main.qml

find:
          // would put this dead station on hours later.
          if (!_mayKnock(root._healRetryAttempts)) { _orderSpent(); return; }

replace:
          // would put this dead station on hours later.
          if (!_mayKnock(root._healRetryAttempts)) { return; }

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_a_spent_budget_takes_the_standing_order_down_with_it.
  Line-neutral.
